          // forever (~500k-trap budget burn / 12s hang). The wait routine passes the awaited
          // event as two OSType fields at [A6+0x8]/[A6+0xC]; it reads the arrived event's two
          // fields from frame locals [A6-0x2C]/[A6-0x28] (which alias the event buffer it passed)
          // and loops until BOTH match. Echo the awaited pair back so the compare succeeds.
          // NOTE: this only stops the HANG. The 20 "4.0" modules that use this (Flying Toasters!,
          // Fish World, Hula Twins, ... all carry a 'cfrg'/'pwpc' PowerPC fragment) then issue
          // ZERO 68K QuickDraw traps — their renderer is the PowerPC fragment, which the 68K host
          // cannot execute. They stay blank here and belong on the PowerPC adhost. ADNOOSD3A opts out.
